      "writtenOn": "2025-04-13T12:34:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Answering myself as I can see it used in I44c6d9e1e4 - it can still be done by having:\n_interface definition_\n```\npublic interface ChangeNumberVirtualIdAlgorithm {\n\n  /**\n   * Convert a serverId/legacyChangeNum tuple into a virtual numeric id\n   *\n   * @param serverId Gerrit serverId\n   * @param legacyChangeNum legacy change number\n   * @return virtual id which combines serverId and legacyChangeNum together\n   */\n  Change.Id apply(String serverId, Change.Id legacyChangeNum);\n  \n  default Change.Id apply(Provider\u003cString\u003e toServerID, Change.Id legacyChangeNum) {\n    return apply(toServerID.get(), legacyChangeNum);\n  }\n}\n```\n\n_`ChangeNumberBitmapMaskAlgorithm` remains unchanged_\n\n_`ChangeNumberNoopAlgorithm` becomes_\n```\n@Singleton\npublic class ChangeNumberNoopAlgorithm implements ChangeNumberVirtualIdAlgorithm {\n  @Override\n  public Change.Id apply(String unused, Change.Id legacyChangeNum) {\n    return legacyChangeNum;\n  }\n\n  @Override\n  public Change.Id apply(Provider\u003cString\u003e unused, Change.Id legacyChangeNum) {\n    return legacyChangeNum;\n  }\n}\n```\n\n_finally `ChangeData` usage from the change in question becomes_\n```\n    if (virtualId \u003d\u003d null) {\n      virtualId \u003d virtualIdFunc.apply(changeServerId(), legacyId);\n    }\n    return virtualId;\n```\n\nclean, without any conditions as they determined on startup (though server configuration existence)...\n\nWDYT?",
